  "graph": {
    "name": "Zigbang: A Hybrid API of Serverless and ECS, Infra as a Code via CDK",
    "link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0F7KDLz-kIQ",
    "categories": "interactive",
    "graph_usable": true,
    "notes": "\"Hybrid architecture with duplexing\"\n    Initially, only Lambda. Due to traffic and cost issues, started operating with ECS/Fargate.\n    Uses 2 route53. The internal one is used to route requests to either the fargate cluster or ApiGateway. Internal route53 is used for weight distrubtion.\n    Used Lambda to read CloudWatch logs and get load information. (building custom autoscaling mechanisms.)\n    ECS insufficient to handle bursty traffic. Used lambda (\"in order to prevent traffic loss during autoscaling\"). while ECS was scaling out.\n    Future: microservice architecture."
  },
